he rounding.\n\nLet me use 2 runes with 1-year, 1 prior contract → 57.5 → 58.\n\nActually, I realize I want to test both halves of the rounding behavior:\n1. Premium fraction → round up (MHPCO's favor)\n2. Payout fraction → round down (MHPCO's favor)\n\nThe payout rounding is in claim.spec.ts. The premium rounding is here.\n\nLet me activate the test.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Red -- Test 22: premium rounding (197.5 → 198)"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_32873b80029841d0bd3ac483","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"    it(\"premium calculation that yields a fraction rounds UP (MHPCO's favor)\", () => {\n      // 2 runes + 1-year customer + 1 prior contract:\n      // base 50, first insurance 10, follow-up = -15% × 50 = -7.5\n      // Total: 50 + 10 - 7.5 + 5 = 57.5 → ceil 58\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 1, contractCount: 1 };\n      expect(calculatePremium(\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        customer,\n      )).toBe(58);\n    });","oldText":"    it.todo(\"premium of 197.5 G rounds UP to 198 G (MHPCO's favor)\");"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_21-00-58_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"    it(\\\"premium calculation that yields a fraction rounds UP (MHPCO's favor)\\\", () => {\\n      // 2 runes + 1-year customer + 1 prior contract:\\n      // base 50, first insurance 10, follow-up = -15% × 50 = -7.5\\n      // Total: 50 + 10 - 7.5 + 5 = 57.5 → ceil 58\\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 1, contractCount: 1 };\\n      expect(calculatePremium(\\n        [{ type: \\\"rune\\\" }, { type: \\\"rune\\\" }],\\n        customer,\\n      )).toBe(58);\\n    });\", \"oldText\": \"    it.todo(\\\"premium of 197.5 G rounds UP to 198 G (MHPCO's favor)\\\");\"}], \"path\": \"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_21-00-58_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2","streamIndex":0}],"api":"openai-completions","pro