al + firstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount + 5\n\nSo adjustedTotal + firstInsurance - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount = 192.5\n\nIf we set up the math to get 192.5, we'd have 192.5 + 5 = 197.5 → 198.\n\nLet me think about what combination gives that.\n\nActually the spec example \"197.5 → 198\" is just illustrative. My test can use a different value. Let me just use 1 rune with 1-year, 1 prior contract:\n- 25 + 2.5 - 3.75 + 5 = 28.75 → ceil 29\n\nActually let me use 3 runes with 1-year, 1 prior:\n- base = 75 (raw, no block... wait, 3 runes with block: base = 60)\n- adjusted = 60 (block applied)\n- first insurance = 10% × 60 × 3 = 18\n- follow-up = -15% × 60 = -9\n- Total: 60 + 18 - 9 + 5 = 74\n\nHmm no fraction.\n\nLet me think differently. Use 4 runes with 1-year, 1 prior:\n- base = 100 (no block)\n- first insurance = 40\n- follow-up = -15\n- Total: 100 + 40 - 15 + 5 = 130\n\nNo fraction.\n\nUse 2 amulets (base 120) with 1-year, 1 prior:\n- adjusted = 120\n- first insurance = 24\n- follow-up = -18\n- Total: 120 + 24 - 18 + 5 = 131\n\nNo fraction.\n\nHmm. Use 1 amulet (base 60) with 1-year, 1 prior:\n- adjusted = 60\n- first insurance = 6\n- follow-up = -9\n- Total: 60 + 6 - 9 + 5 = 62\n\nNo fraction.\n\nUse 2 potions (base 80) with 1-year, 1 prior:\n- adjusted = 80\n- first insurance = 16\n- follow-up = -12\n- Total: 80 + 16 - 12 + 5 = 89\n\nNo fraction.\n\nUse 1 sword enchantment 5 (base 100, adjusted 130) with 1-year, 1 prior:\n- adjusted = 130\n- first insurance = 10\n- follow-up = -15\n- Total: 130 + 10 - 15 + 5 = 130\n\nNo fraction.\n\nI need base that's not a multiple of 5 or 10 to get a fraction. Components are 25 each, so multiples of 25 are easy. With 1 rune: base 25, follow-up = 3.75. With 2 runes: base 50, follow-up = 7.5.\n\nLet me try 2 runes with 1-year, 1 prior:\n- adjusted = 50 (no block)\n- first insurance = 10% × 50 × 2 = 10\n- follow-up = -7.5\n- Total: 50 + 10 - 7.5 + 5 = 57.5 → ceil 58\n\nYes! This gives 57.5 → 58.\n\nLet me use this for the rounding test.\n\nActually wait, I want to be careful. Let me check the spec example values.\n\nThe spec says: \"a premium calculation that yields 197.5 G → final premium 198 G (rounded up)\". This is illustrative. My test can use any value that exercises the rounding.\n\nLet me use 2 runes with 1-year, 1 prior contract → 57.5 → 58.\n\nActually, I realize I want to test both halves of the rounding behavior:\n1. Premium fraction → round up (MHPCO's favor)\n2. Payout fraction → round down (MHPCO's favor)\n\nThe payout rounding is in claim.spec.ts. The premium rounding is here.\n\nLet me activate the test.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Red -- Test 22: premium rounding (197.5 → 198)"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_32873b80029841d0bd3ac483","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"    it(\"premium calculation that yields a fraction rounds UP (MHPCO's favor)\", () => {\n      // 2 runes + 1-year customer + 1 prior contract:\n      // base 50, first insurance 10, follow-up = -15% × 50 = -7.5\n      // Total: 50 + 10 - 7.5 + 5 = 57.5 → ceil 58\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 1, contractCount: 1 };\n      expect(calculatePremium(\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        customer,\n      )).toBe(58);\n    });","oldText":"    it.todo(\"premium of 197.5 G rounds UP to 198 G (MHPCO's favor)\");"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_21-00-58_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-clean"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"    it(\\\"premium calculation that yields a fraction rounds UP (MHPCO's favor)\\\", () => {\\n      // 2 runes + 1-year customer + 1 prior contract:\\n      // base 50, first insurance 10, follow-up = -15% × 50 = -7.5\\n      // Total: 50 + 10 - 7.5 + 5 = 57.5 → ceil 58\\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 1, contractCount: 1 };\\n      expect(calculatePremium(\\n        [{ type: \\\"rune\\\" }, { type: \\\"rune\\\" }],\\n        customer,\\n      )).toBe(58);\\n    });\", \"oldText\": \"    it.todo(\\\"premium of 197.5 G rounds UP to 198 G (MHPCO's favor)\\\");\"}], \"path\": \"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_21-00-58_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-clean","streamIndex":0}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784933945866,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-197a2685-63a6-464e-be53-278d65c4ed40","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"}}
